# Test: redistribute-late-consumer -- a consumer that registers after a producer
#       emitted holds that producer's current route set.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-redistribution-chain-drops-silently AC-3, at the process
# boundary. The orchestrator dispatches over the consumer registry read LIVE at
# event time (handleBatch, internal/component/bgp/plugins/redistribute_egress/
# redistribute.go), so a batch emitted one moment before a consumer registered
# reached every consumer except that one and was lost with no line in any log.
# A consumer becoming registered now fires a replay request of its own, every
# producer re-emits its current set, and the answer is injected through that
# consumer.
#
# PREVENTS: the outcome depending on which plugin started first. The static
# plugin and the IS-IS plugin start in the SAME startup tier and nothing orders
# them, which is why isis-redist-frr was red while its adjacency was green.
#
# THE ORDER IS THE TEST. The observer emits 10.99.0.0/24 while no consumer named
# `fakedest` exists, and registers the consumer afterwards. Nothing else can
# deliver that route: the incremental dispatch already ran, over a registry that
# did not hold this consumer.
#
# `fakeprobe` is registered first and exists to make that claim mean something.
# The orchestrator subscribes to its producers on a goroutine, so an emit that
# reached nobody would look exactly like a late consumer that was never
# replayed. The scenario emits 10.98.0.0/24 and WAITS for the probe to hold it,
# which proves the dispatcher is listening before the measured emit happens.
#
# The answer is read ONCE, with no settle window, because the replay is
# synchronous on the in-process bus. A daemon that needs to be waited for here
# is delivering by some other path, which is a different behavior wearing this
# test's name.
#
# No peer and no port: `destination fakedest` puts nothing on a BGP session, so
# this scenario needs no session at all.

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external redist-late-consumer-test {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/redistribute-late-consumer"
		encoder json
	}
	internal fakeredist {
		use fakeredist
	}
}

redistribute {
	# The probe: registered first, and the proof that the dispatcher is live.
	destination fakeprobe {
		import fakeredist {
			family [ ipv4/unicast ];
		}
	}
	# The late consumer: registered after both emits.
	destination fakedest {
		import fakeredist {
			family [ ipv4/unicast ];
		}
	}
}

bgp {
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=25s
expect=exit:code=0
